From 27a0cb47786888834e15fdcf683c185e031a66b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:57:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 240/252] perf(cpu-avx2): execute broadcast natively
 (avx2-broadcast-native)

The AVX2 backend had no native broadcast plane: every broadcast plan was
declared host_reference and executed through the vector-common Python
reference, which was the single largest remaining fallback surface of the
Qwen3.5-0.8B AVX2 prefill path (~39 s of ~109 s at T=5, 494 calls).

Port the verified AVX-512 reference design:

- cpu_avx2.py: emit ptx_avx2_broadcast_f32/bf16.  The contract predicate
  (broadcast_native_contract) accepts standard same-dtype expansion with
  input dim 1 or equal to the output dim, one tensor/scalar input, rank <=
  16, and expresses it as per-output-axis input strides.  The runtime and
  the artifact metadata share the predicate, and every non-native broadcast
  carries an explicit native_broadcast_fallback_operations reason.
- backends/cpu/x86/avx2.py: dispatch the native kernel and validate the
  contract, input count, rank and output count before the call.
- f32/bf16 lanes use integer bit quieting so signaling-NaN payloads match
  the host reference's Python-float round trip byte for byte; finite,
  subnormal, infinity, zero and quiet-NaN patterns are unchanged.
- broadcast leaves host_preexpanded_operations (now only where) and is
  declared through native_broadcast_mode / native_broadcast_operations /
  native_helper_symbols.
- Wire/compat: ARTIFACT_PAYLOAD_VERSION 5 -> 6 and NATIVE_ABI_MARKER /
  ptx_avx2_abi pypto-x.cpu.avx2:6 -> :7.  Stale payload/ABI artifacts are
  rejected fail-closed; the emitted source digest changes, so the
  content-addressed cache cannot silently reuse a pre-broadcast object.
  AVX2_LOWERING_VERSION stays 2 because the vector plan wire is unchanged
  (same version-chain shape as the AVX-512 B6 / AVX2 PXLD-v2 waves).

Tests: new test_cpu_avx2_broadcast.py covers Qwen3.5 broadcast shapes plus
rank 0/1..5/16, identity, scalar source, odd/tail and empty axes, f32/bf16
bitwise differentials against a pure stdlib oracle and the real
host-reference path, non-native dtype (int8..uint64/bool) and rank>16
fallback declarations, mixed-dtype/dimension predicate rejection,
non-contiguous descriptor rejection, declared==dispatched kernel spy,
payload/ABI/metadata tamper rejection and an nm symbol guard.  Existing
payload/ABI assertions were bumped to 6/:7.
